**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests`

**How to implement.** A study persists as its own kit file, `<name>.study-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema, and recording it snapshots and pins the material versions it opens (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .study-json'; 001 §E 'Library closure snapshot', 'Writes are atomic'; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … studies'; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`) and step 217's shape for items; no second parser or writer is written. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `Studies.fs`, after `Study` (step 358): `StudyFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; study : Study }`, the `.study-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1; `type Study with member this.studyFile : StudyFile` (one direction, ELEV006); and `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`, each opened material's `EntryVersionReference { entryId = version.materialId.toLibraryEntryId; version = version.version }` in study order (steps 24, 137): what the kit snapshots and pins. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/item.schema.json` (step 217), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/study.json`: `schemaVersion` a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 (`then`), the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `study`, and `study` holds exactly `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\S`), `experiments` (an array of non-empty strings), `materials`, `scopes`, `links` and `sessionGains` (arrays), `settings` (an object holding exactly `mode`, an integer from 1 to 2, `experimentWeights` and `detectorWeights`, arrays, and `disabled`, an array of non-empty strings) and `notes` (a string). The inner shapes are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/item.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateStudyFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateItemFile` (step 217) does. (3) `CanonicalJson.options` (`CanonicalJson.fs`) gains two converters, for `ParameterScope` and `FitMode`, written as step 285's `ExperimentRole` converter is and registered beside it before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: each writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `SessionGainModel`, `StudyParameterRef` and `CrystalParameters` keep the serializer's case form, and nothing else in the options changes. (4) `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146, 217-219): `type StudyFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`); `type KitFileText with member this.parseStudyFile : Result<StudyFile, StorageError>` (`parseVersionedText validateStudyFile StudyKitFile.extension StudyFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`, steps 123-124); on the `KitProxy` extension `member this.writeStudy (study : Study) : Result<unit, KitError>`, which writes `study.studyFile.fileText` with `writeKindFile StudyKitFile study.name.fileStem`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, and `member this.readStudies () : Result<Study list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles StudyKitFile` answers, a refusal or a file whose study's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason and refusing the whole read, ordered by the name's text (ordinal); and on the `KitLibraryContext` extension `member this.recordStudy (study : Study) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`: `this.snapshotReferences study.libraryReferences` (step 139), then `this.kit.proxy.writeStudy study`, a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeStudy` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. No delete, rename, cache or other member is added. There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. (5) Tests. Their study is test-local: `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, with an opened absorbing crystal material written as an `OpenedMaterial` record literal over a test-local probe whose one parameter, `n3`, is an `UnknownParameter` with a prior, one `ScopedParameter` (`ExperimentScope`), one `ParameterLink`, one gain setting of each `SessionGainModel` case, both weights, E2 disabled and two lines of notes. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `a study is stored under its name`: `StudyKitFile.fileNameOf (StudyName "QZ-LR").fileStem` is `FileName "QZ-LR.study-json"`; `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`: `studyFile`, `fileText`, `parseStudyFile` answer an equal file; the text holds no `\r`, ends with exactly one `\n`, lists its top-level keys as `schemaVersion` then `study` in ordinal order, writes the fit mode and the scope as their tags, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text; `a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` 2, with its body and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = StudyKitFile.extension`, found 2 and expected 1; `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds`: without `study`, with an extra top-level key, with `study.name` `"  "` and with `study.settings.mode` 3 each answer `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166, 285): `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `ParameterScope` and `FitMode` as its tag (`SessionBlockScope` as `3`) and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the scope tag 5 and the mode tag 3 with `MalformedJsonErr`. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs`, `module KitStudyFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "KitStudyFileTests", <a new GUID>)` and a `KitProxy.create` over it with `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 218's precedent): `a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name`: `QZ-LR` and `LR` written answer `LR.study-json` and `QZ-LR.study-json` in the folder and `readStudies` answers `LR` then `QZ-LR`; `a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file`: `Broken.study-json` holding `{` and `Other.study-json` holding `QZ-LR`'s text each make `readStudies` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file; `a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView` `writeStudy` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and the folder's bytes are unchanged. `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its built-in library, its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write: `recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file`: a user absorbing crystal material saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial` and held by `QZ-LR` as an `OpenedMaterial` record literal of its version, recorded through `recordStudy`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding that material's version 1 and its category, `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.material-json` and `QZ-LR.study-json`, the recorder holding that version, and `kit.proxy.readStudies ()` answering the study; `a read-only kit records no study`: under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` `recordStudy` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the study file lands, `StudyFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseStudyFile` reads back equal against `schema/study.schema.json`, `KitProxy.writeStudy` / `readStudies` MUST store each study under its name and refuse a bad file whole, and `KitLibraryContext.recordStudy` MUST snapshot and pin the opened material versions before it writes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study is stored under its name`, `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds`, `a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name`, `a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file`, `a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing`, `recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file` and `a read-only kit records no study`, the count rising by 9, and the widened `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
